# Refactor ownership

The WebApi and `web` refactor runs in phases (P0 foundations, P1 contracts, P2 schema kit, P3 backend core, P4
dimensions pilot, P5 module waves, P6 integration). The spec is `docs/blueprint/`; the contract is
`api/openapi/contract/` (see its README). The **integrator** is the main session; it merges every branch.

## Branches and worktrees

- Each agent works in its own git worktree on `refactor/<phase>/<module>` (for example `refactor/p1/dimensions`,
  `refactor/p5/datasets`), cut from the current phase base (`feature/web2-refactor` after the previous gate). The
  schema agent works on a branch in the `database/srdb_ebm` repository.
- Commit only files you own. Never merge, rebase onto or cherry-pick another agent's branch; the integrator merges in
  a fixed order and rebases waiting branches.

## Who writes what

| Owner | Writes | Everything else |
|---|---|---|
| Integrator | `api/openapi/contract/admin-api.yaml`, `common.yaml`, `redocly.yaml`, `compose.mjs`, `plugins/`; `web/src/lib/api/*`; `web/src/app/*` (router, layout) and `web/src/components/app-sidebar.tsx`; `WebApi/Program.cs`, shared `WebApi/Configuration/` extensions, `WebApi/Errors/`; `Application/Changes/`, `Versioning/` core, `Metadata/`, `Vocabulary/` core; `tests/.../Support`, `tests/.../Errors`, contract tests; `docs/blueprint/*`; root `package.json`; this file | — |
| Module agent `<m>` | `api/openapi/contract/<m>.yaml`; its Application and WebApi feature folders (below) and its own `<Feature>ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs`; Infrastructure files for its new tables; its `tests/.../<Feature>/**`; `web/src/lib/<m>/**`; `web/src/components/<m>/**` | Read-only: other modules' folders, the shared kernel, everything the integrator owns |
| Schema agent | `database/srdb_ebm/**` | Read-only: the Admin repo |

| Module `<m>` | Blueprint | Feature folders (Application, WebApi, tests) | `web` folders |
|---|---|---|---|
| `tenant` | 10 | `Session`, `Tenancy`, `SystemTenants`, `Overview`, `Development` | `lib/tenant`, `lib/session` |
| `datasets` | 11 | `Datasets`, `Bindings`, `Measures`, `SourceObjects` | `lib/datasets`, `components/datasets` |
| `dimensions` | 12 | `Dimensions` | `lib/dimensions`, `components/dimensions` |
| `mappings` | 13 | `Mappings`, `Bridges` | `lib/mappings`, `components/mappings` |
| `releases` | 14 | `Releases`, `AssumptionSets` | `lib/releases`, `components/releases`, `components/assumption-sets` |
| `models` | 15 | `CalculationModels`, `Expressions` | `lib/models` (new), `lib/model`, `components/models` |
| `reports` | 16 | `Reports`, `ReportEditor` | `lib/reports` (new), `lib/report`, `components/reports`, `components/report` |

A folder not listed belongs to the integrator.

## Cross-module needs

A module that needs another module's data or behavior (reports writing report bridges, releases reading dataset
versions) calls that module's public Application service. It never edits the other module's folder or contract file.
A missing hook, a missing shared type in `common.yaml` or `lib/api`, or a change to an integrator-owned file is a
written request to the integrator in the agent's report, with the exact change needed.

## Shared hotspots (settled by the integrator)

- **Contract tags and module files:** fixed in `admin-api.yaml`; a module only edits `<m>.yaml`. Component names are
  global across contract files, so prefix them with the module's entities (`DimensionListItem`).
- **Vocabularies:** each module adds its own vocabulary file, found by discovery; nobody edits `VocabularyCatalog.cs`.
- **DI registration:** each module registers through its own `<Feature>ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs`.
- **`web` navigation:** routes and the sidebar belong to the integrator; request entries.
- **Generated files:** `api/openapi/contract/bundled.yaml`, `web/src/lib/api/schema.d.ts` and
  `api/openapi/admin-api.json` are regenerated, never hand-edited or hand-merged.

## Done checks before handing back

From the repo root: `pnpm contract:lint` and `pnpm contract:bundle`. From `web/`: `pnpm contract:types`,
`pnpm build`, `pnpm lint`. From P3 on, also `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` in `api/`.
